<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Wadi al-Khaznadar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1299">1299</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Wadi al-Khaznadar was fought in 1299 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homs">Homs</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazan-khan">Ghazan Khan</a> defeated the army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a>. It was the only major Mongol victory in the long conflict between the two powers. Logistical difficulties prevented the Ilkhanate from turning the success into lasting territorial gains.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-wadi-al-khaznadar.jpg" alt="Battle of Wadi al-Khaznadar" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BattleOfHoms1299.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
